// LSP M3.5 workspace-indexing fixture — the THIRD half, and the one that keeps `--project` meaningful.
//
// widget.kama and app.kama share a folder, so they are ONE module (SPEC.md § Modules: a module
// is a folder, not a declaration) and a query on either already sees the other. What a member-file query
// cannot see is a DIFFERENT module of the same project — this file, listed as `parts` in kama.json — and
// widening to every module under the nearest kama.json is exactly what `--project` is for.
import { wsproj::Widget };

fn int32 partSize(Widget w) { return w.size; }
